<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S5.T2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Probing for Misalignment.</span> To quantify increase in potentially harmful behaviors between the base model and the trained models, we use probes, which we implement using <span id="S5.T2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gpt-4o</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Given an <span id="S5.T2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">anchor</span> object, <math id="S5.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, and the <span id="S5.T2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">message</span> generated by the agent, <math id="S5.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, we query <span id="S5.T2.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gpt-4o</span> to find whether there are safety concerns about the generated message. We evaluate generations from the baseline, RFT, and TFB independently. After running the probes, we compute the percentage of harmful behaviors detected for each model, which we present in <span id="S5.T2.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Abs.</span> column. Finally, we examine the relative increases in harmful behavior, which we report in the <math id="S5.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\%</annotation></semantics></math> columns. The prompts used for each of the five probes are presented in Appendix <a href="#A8" title="Appendix H Probes ‣ Moloch’s Bargain: Emergent Misalignment When LLMs Compete for Audiences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span></a>. The reported results represent the average across three runs of the probe. Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B All Probes ‣ Moloch’s Bargain: Emergent Misalignment When LLMs Compete for Audiences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> provides the detailed results for each run. The results are robust, with standard deviations reported in Table <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ A.2 Misalignment Probes Across Two Audiences ‣ Appendix A Results Across Two Audiences ‣ Moloch’s Bargain: Emergent Misalignment When LLMs Compete for Audiences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</figcaption>
