<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Results Across Two Audiences</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Performance Across Two Audiences</h3>

<figure id="A1.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Same as Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Moloch’s Bargain: Emergent Misalignment When LLMs Compete for Audiences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, with both biographic and demographic audiences.</figcaption>
<div id="A1.T7.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:94pt;vertical-align:-45.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-60.8pt,14.4pt) scale(0.765737079056747,0.765737079056747) ;">
<table id="A1.T7.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T7.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"></th>
