<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Misalignment Probes Across Two Audiences</h3>

<figure id="A1.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span><span id="A1.T8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Misalignment Probes.</span> Probing for model misalignment. <math id="A1.T8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>% and Std (%) denote the mean change and standard deviation across all probes. Results are averaged over three runs, with detailed outcomes provided in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B All Probes ‣ Moloch’s Bargain: Emergent Misalignment When LLMs Compete for Audiences" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>. <span id="A1.T8.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Avg.</span> indicates the average shift, while <span id="A1.T8.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Norm Avg.</span> represents the normalized average (mean divided by standard deviation), quantifying how many standard deviations away from no change the effect lies. Overall, we observe a significant shift toward misaligned behavior on average across both audiences, though the trends are not consistent across all probes.</figcaption>
<div id="A1.T8.8" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:149.1pt;vertical-align:-72.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-58.2pt,21.8pt) scale(0.773359266376787,0.773359266376787) ;">
<table id="A1.T8.8.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
